# JARVIS -- KLIMS Hospital Voice Assistant
## Setup & Deployment Guide

A voice/chat assistant with RAG over a hospital knowledge base (Pinecone),
Hindi/English support, appointment booking with email confirmation, and a
React frontend talking to a FastAPI backend.

---

## 1. Prerequisites

| Requirement | Version / Notes |
|---|---|
| Python | **3.11.15 -- required. Newer versions (3.13+) lack prebuilt wheels for `pyaudio` and other native deps used in this project. |
| Node.js | 18+ (for the Vite/React frontend) |
| Conda | Recommended for managing the Python environment cleanly |
| Windows only | Confirm **Smart App Control** is **Off** (Settings -> Privacy & security -> Windows Security -> App & browser control). If On, it blocks native DLLs several dependencies need (`jiter`, `xxhash`, etc.) with cryptic `ImportError` messages. This is a one-way switch -- no re-enabling without a clean Windows reinstall. |

Accounts/keys you'll need:
- **Hugging Face** account + access token (for the LLM via HF Inference Providers, and for embeddings)
- **Pinecone** account + API key (free tier) -- vector database for the hospital PDF
- **Gmail** account with an **App Password** (not your normal password) -- for booking confirmation emails. Generate one at https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords (requires 2-Step Verification enabled first)

